findings.scenario:
The code's own doc lists `a unit (Referat II.3, Abteilung VI.4)` as a name, and the near-miss test pins that. But SECTION_LOCATORS (taken from TED's 23-language template) includes words that mean department or unit in their languages, and a Locator may open a Label.

The probe returned srp=true and Placeholder for:
- `Afdeling II.3`, `Afd. VI.4` and `afd. II.1` (DA/NL "department");
- `Oddelek II.3` (SL "department");
- `Oddiel II.3` and `Oddíl II.3` (SK/CS);
- `Sekcja II.1` (PL);
- `Sezione II.1` and `Sez. II.1` (IT court or unit section);
- `Τμήμα II.3` (EL "department");
- `Abschnitt II.3`, `Kapitel II.3`, `Avsnitt II.3` and `Afsnit II.3`.

The German equivalents `Referat II.3`, `Abteilung VI.4`, `Abt. VI.4` and `Dezernat V.1` stay names. Generic office titles behave the same way: `Vergabestelle IV.2`, `Kontaktstelle II.1`, `Auftraggeber V.1` and `Aanbestedende dienst II.3` all give Placeholder.

A party drops only if all its names do, so this needs a sub-unit designation to be the party's whole published name: uncommon, but it is the case the doc says unit 5 keeps. In dry 2283 no changed Label fold opens with any of these words; only English `Section` opens one (`Section VI.4.2) below` 23 orgs, `Section II.1.4` 1, `SECTION VI: …` 1).

None of the near misses that pinned these guards opens with a pointer word, so `pointer_led` alone now keeps each of them:
- ORG-1 `Müller Bau GmbH (siehe Abschnitt VI.3)` (legal form);
- ORG-2 `Consortium … listed in VI.3 below` (over 12 words);
- ORG-4 EN `Siemens Healthcare (VI.3)` (same language);
- all 16 names in partyname.rs:3373's `!translation_shaped(party)` list;
- `!translation_shaped("Acme AS VI.3")` in `the_pointer_word_as_is_no_legal_form`.

So you can delete `!names_a_legal_form(raw) &&` or the `TRANSLATION_MAX_WORDS` cap from `translation_shaped`, or the `*from != lang` test from `translation_echoes`, and every test stays green. Each deletion drops a real party. For example: EN_VI3 plus DE `Siehe Abschnitt VI.3 Müller Bau GmbH`. That copy is `None`, because the only German stem is ` siehe oben`. It is pointer-led, so only the legal-form guard keeps the party. Likewise EN_VI3 plus EN `See VI.3 Siemens Healthcare` (`None`, since ` see section` doesn't match) is kept only by the label test.

findings.fix:
Rewrite ORG-1, ORG-2 and ORG-4 as pointer-led copies whose only keeper is the guard:
