Add premise asserts that `not_a_name(copy) == None` and that the copy is pointer-led. Add pointer-led legal-form names (`Se punkt VI.3 Hansen A/S`, `Voir point VI.3 Dupont SARL`, `Wie VI.3 Acme plc`) and a long pointer-led name to partyname.rs's negative `translation_shaped` list.

findings.scenario:
Every negative case in `a_name_beside_a_section_reference_stays_a_name` holds a word outside the closed lists (`Krajowa`, `Referat`, `Acme`, `date`, `is`). So `reference_shape` rejects them before any of these guards is reached:
- the opener restriction (a joiner, noun, position or notice word cannot open);
- `Number` only right after a locator;
- lead-ins only first;
- no pointer after a reference;
- `section_reference`'s legal-form check (`!legal_form_reading(raw, true)`).

Removing any one of them leaves all tests green. The legal-form check is only reachable by a dotted form made of list words. For example, `S.p.A. VI.3` reads as `s` pointer, `p` locator, `a` joiner, then the reference. Only `company_token` (`SpA`) keeps it a name.
